  "title": "Coast Guard conducts highseas medevac off Elizabeth City, NC",
  "description": "B-roll of Crew members from Coast Guard Air Station Elizabeth City, N.C., conduct a medevac of a 55-year-old Croatian man from aboard the 516-foot motor vessel Orange Wave approximately 200 miles east of Elizabeth City, N.C., Jan. 13, 2011. Watchstanders at the Coast Guard 5th District Command Center launched crewmembers from Coast Guard Air Station Elizabeth City, N.C., aboard an MH-60 Jayhawk helicopter to perform the medevac and a C-130 Hercules to assist with communications. U.S. Coast Guard video. Produced by Senior Chief Petty Officer Steve Carleton.",
